What's wrong?

264
00:19:22,065 --> 00:19:23,265
Rehearsal not going well?

265
00:19:38,145 --> 00:19:40,905
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

266
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:05,745
Did something happen?

267
00:20:06,345 --> 00:20:08,105
It's not me. It's the keyboard player.

268
00:20:08,705 --> 00:20:09,905
His dad came today,

269
00:20:09,985 --> 00:20:12,025
took all the instruments, and beat him up.

270
00:20:13,825 --> 00:20:15,545
Why are adults always like this?

271
00:20:15,625 --> 00:20:17,225
Why can't they support our dreams?

272
00:20:17,305 --> 00:20:18,985
Didn't they have dreams
when they were young?

273
00:20:26,265 --> 00:20:28,865
Maybe when they chased their dreams,

274
00:20:28,945 --> 00:20:30,505
they stumbled too many times,

275
00:20:30,585 --> 00:20:32,905
so they don't want you
to go through the same thing.

276
00:20:33,505 --> 00:20:35,625
Whether his dad has dreams, I don't know,

277
00:20:35,705 --> 00:20:37,665
but my dad definitely doesn't have any.

278
00:20:38,265 --> 00:20:39,945
Otherwise, my mom wouldn't
have gotten so mad, she left home.

279
00:20:53,305 --> 00:20:58,265
BANK

280
00:21:32,105 --> 00:21:34,145
CONTACT: YUN, MAKE A CALL?

281
00:21:36,585 --> 00:21:37,425
CONTACT: YUN

282
00:21:37,505 --> 00:21:41,345
CALLING YUN

283
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:42,265
END CALL

284
00:22:33,145 --> 00:22:35,385
-What are you doing?
-Noise. Disturbing the peace.

285
00:22:35,985 --> 00:22:37,865
Leave my room immediately.

286
00:22:37,945 --> 00:22:38,985
He.

287
00:22:45,625 --> 00:22:47,265
Look at her,
acting completely out of control.

288
00:22:47,345 --> 00:22:48,825
Take it easy.

289
00:22:49,345 --> 00:22:50,465
Leave it to me.

290
00:23:16,985 --> 00:23:18,865
How did you do that?
What did you say to her?

291
00:23:19,545 --> 00:23:21,225
Nothing much.
Just gave her a pair of headphones.

292
00:23:24,265 --> 00:23:25,105
Eat first.

293
00:23:25,865 --> 00:23:27,145
There's more in the pot
if it's not enough.

294
00:23:33,345 --> 00:23:35,185
Let's talk business.
I'll brief you on the case.

295
00:23:36,105 --> 00:23:37,545
The Forensic Department

296
00:23:37,625 --> 00:23:40,505
found signs of arsenic poisoning
in Xu Zhihong's skull.

297
00:23:41,145 --> 00:23:42,985
At the Xu residence,

298
00:23:43,065 --> 00:23:44,585
I found some herbal residue.

299
00:23:45,385 --> 00:23:46,545
I've already handed it over to Liang Juan.

300
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:49,545
The test report should be out tomorrow.

301
00:23:51,305 --> 00:23:52,305
Zhang…

302
00:23:55,305 --> 00:23:56,625
Zhang Ersong.

303
00:23:56,705 --> 00:23:57,665
Who?

304
00:23:59,945 --> 00:24:02,385
Master Zhang from 1713 Qihuang Clinic.

305
00:24:02,465 --> 00:24:04,865
This should be the prescription
he gave Xu Zhihong.

306
00:24:04,945 --> 00:24:06,865
I found out Xu Zhihong
once had a huge argument

307
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:07,905
with Zhang Ersong.

308
00:24:07,985 --> 00:24:09,185
He even threatened to expose him.

309
00:24:09,265 --> 00:24:11,385
The two fell out badly.

310
00:24:11,465 --> 00:24:12,905
Zhang Ersong

311
00:24:13,825 --> 00:24:14,705
deliberately poisoned him?

312
00:24:21,345 --> 00:24:24,665
<i>The skin of mung beans is green.</i>
<i>It belongs to wood.</i>

313
00:24:24,745 --> 00:24:25,425
QIGONG MASTER, ZHANG ERSONG

314
00:24:25,945 --> 00:24:29,065
<i>When boiled into soup, it turns yellow,</i>
<i>which belongs to earth.</i>

315
00:24:29,145 --> 00:24:30,745
<i>This spirited,</i>

316
00:24:30,825 --> 00:24:32,785
<i>energetic elderly gentleman</i>

317
00:24:32,865 --> 00:24:34,705
<i>is the renowned healer of Beijing,</i>

318
00:24:34,785 --> 00:24:36,225
<i>a third generation inheritor,</i>

319
00:24:36,305 --> 00:24:38,185
<i>Master Zhang Ersong.</i>

320
00:24:38,265 --> 00:24:40,145
<i>Mung beans and eggplant,</i>

321
00:24:40,745 --> 00:24:42,505
<i>together complete the five elements.</i>

322
00:24:43,025 --> 00:24:47,305
THE MEDICINAL DREGS DELIVERED YESTERDAY
CONTAINED TRACE ARSENIC.

323
00:24:49,105 --> 00:24:50,905
<i>Songbentang Traditional Medicine Clinic</i>

324
00:24:50,985 --> 00:24:54,545
<i>was founded by Master Zhang Ersong,</i>

325
00:24:54,625 --> 00:24:56,825
<i>a third generation healer of Beijing.</i>

326
00:24:57,425 --> 00:24:58,705
-<i>Master Zhang Ersong</i>
-Zhang Ersong.

327
00:24:58,785 --> 00:25:00,705
<i>is like Hua Tuo reborn.</i>

328
00:25:00,785 --> 00:25:01,745
What are you here for?

329
00:25:02,265 --> 00:25:03,945
-Registration number?
-What number?

330
00:25:04,825 --> 00:25:06,625
To see Master Zhang, you need to register.

331
00:25:06,705 --> 00:25:08,345
This number should work, right?

332
00:25:08,425 --> 00:25:09,345
I don't care who you are.

333
00:25:09,425 --> 00:25:11,545
Even the mayor has to register.

334
00:25:11,625 --> 00:25:13,505
And Master Zhang is off today,
no consultations.

335
00:25:16,945 --> 00:25:18,065
Zhang Ersong,

336
00:25:18,145 --> 00:25:19,985
a relative from your hometown
in Langzhong is here.

337
00:25:20,065 --> 00:25:21,985
Your home is in Chentang County,

338
00:25:22,065 --> 00:25:24,065
Maquan Township, Wumaganzhi Village.

339
00:25:24,145 --> 00:25:26,505
At 25, you committed fraud
and served time.

340
00:25:26,585 --> 00:25:28,225
-At 28…
-<i>Zhao,</i>

341
00:25:28,905 --> 00:25:30,705
<i>let this patient in.</i>

342
00:25:31,225 --> 00:25:33,425
<i>You can tell at a glance</i>
<i>he's seriously ill.</i>

343
00:25:33,505 --> 00:25:34,345
Alright.

344
00:25:35,905 --> 00:25:37,225
Go on in.

345
00:25:41,265 --> 00:25:42,545
BENEVOLENT HEART, DIVINE HEALING

346
00:25:42,625 --> 00:25:43,865
A MIRACLE HEALER, A BENEVOLENT MASTER

347
00:25:51,265 --> 00:25:52,265
Please have a look, both of you.

348
00:25:53,545 --> 00:25:54,545
WEIYANG PEOPLE'S HOSPITAL
MEDICAL DIAGNOSIS

349
00:25:54,625 --> 00:25:55,545
Officers,

350
00:25:55,625 --> 00:25:57,625
I've truly been wronged.

351
00:25:57,705 --> 00:26:00,705
The prescription I gave Xu Zhihong

352
00:26:00,785 --> 00:26:03,225
was something I developed
through years of research.

353
00:26:03,305 --> 00:26:05,705
Even now that I'm ill,

354
00:26:05,785 --> 00:26:07,705
I'm still using the same prescription.

355
00:26:10,985 --> 00:26:13,425
What exactly is in
this prescription of yours?

356
00:26:14,025 --> 00:26:16,545
That's a trade secret.

357
00:26:17,065 --> 00:26:18,625
A proprietary formula.

358
00:26:19,425 --> 00:26:22,505
You added a large amount
of realgar to this medicine, didn't you?

359
00:26:23,105 --> 00:26:24,065
How do you know?

360
00:26:25,545 --> 00:26:27,985
Realgar contains a high amount of arsenic.

361
00:26:28,065 --> 00:26:29,545
Long term excessive use

362
00:26:29,625 --> 00:26:31,905
can lead to arsenic poisoning.

363
00:26:32,585 --> 00:26:33,425
You…

364
00:26:33,945 --> 00:26:35,585
You're not trying to fool me, are you?

365
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:40,145
Hospital reports don't lie, do they?

366
00:26:40,825 --> 00:26:43,785
Anyone with basic scientific knowledge
would understand that.

367
00:26:45,545 --> 00:26:47,065
This is the first time I've seen

368
00:26:47,145 --> 00:26:49,185
someone poison others
and not spare himself.

369
00:26:53,825 --> 00:26:54,785
Tell me,

370
00:26:54,865 --> 00:26:57,625
that Xu Zhihong,
why did he want to expose you?

371
00:26:58,585 --> 00:27:01,345
That was due to his frostbite condition.

372
00:27:01,425 --> 00:27:03,105
How would I know?

373
00:27:03,185 --> 00:27:05,545
After Xu Zhihong got the medicine,

374
00:27:05,625 --> 00:27:06,985
he started pestering me,

375
00:27:07,065 --> 00:27:08,825
demanding a refund,

376
00:27:08,905 --> 00:27:10,665
even threatening to go to the media.

377
00:27:10,745 --> 00:27:12,625
You tell me,

378
00:27:12,705 --> 00:27:14,865
how could I not get
into a conflict with him?

379
00:27:16,265 --> 00:27:17,785
A conflict is one thing,

380
00:27:17,865 --> 00:27:20,705
but it wouldn't escalate
to the level of murder.

381
00:27:23,065 --> 00:27:24,105
The key is…

382
00:27:28,905 --> 00:27:31,705
The key is, I already refunded his money.

383
00:27:34,065 --> 00:27:36,145
REFUND RECEIPT

384
00:27:39,505 --> 00:27:41,185
Before you moved out of Yuanlongli,

385
00:27:41,265 --> 00:27:43,105
did you encounter anything unusual?

386
00:27:43,185 --> 00:27:45,225
If you're asking about the case,

387
00:27:45,305 --> 00:27:46,985
I really don't know.

388
00:27:47,065 --> 00:27:49,265
But if you want gossip,

389
00:27:49,345 --> 00:27:50,985
back in those days at Qihuang Clinic,

390
00:27:51,065 --> 00:27:52,505
there was gossip every day.

391
00:27:52,585 --> 00:27:54,545
The property manager, Qian Dajun,

392
00:27:54,625 --> 00:27:56,545
used to moonlight at my place,
reselling appointment slots.

393
00:27:56,625 --> 00:27:58,585
Cripple Du from the steel factory

394
00:27:58,665 --> 00:28:00,465
and Song Qingsong from the cement plant

395
00:28:00,545 --> 00:28:02,945
both came to me for kidney issues.

396
00:28:03,545 --> 00:28:05,825
But Song Qingsong didn't come often.

397
00:28:05,905 --> 00:28:08,025
The membership card he got
was used by his brother-in-law.

398
00:28:08,105 --> 00:28:10,025
And Jin Manshan from Jinsha Market

399
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:12,585
also came to me for heart treatment.

400
00:28:15,665 --> 00:28:17,865
Back then, someone
came to me to practice qigong,

401
00:28:17,945 --> 00:28:21,025
saying he wanted to treat
his strange condition.

402
00:28:21,105 --> 00:28:22,065
A strange condition?

403
00:28:22,145 --> 00:28:24,625
He said he had a peculiar habit.

404
00:28:25,945 --> 00:28:27,625
He couldn't be with women,

405
00:28:27,705 --> 00:28:30,065
yet he liked collecting women's clothing

406
00:28:30,585 --> 00:28:33,665
and watching women's bodies
from a distance.

407
00:28:39,425 --> 00:28:40,425
Who was that person?

408
00:28:41,305 --> 00:28:42,345
I remember now.

409
00:28:42,425 --> 00:28:44,345
Xu Zhihong was introduced by him.

410
00:28:44,425 --> 00:28:46,425
He even said Xu Meng was his god-sister.

411
00:28:47,185 --> 00:28:50,025
You could tell right away
it wasn't a proper relationship.

412
00:28:50,105 --> 00:28:51,465
Who exactly was it?

413
00:28:51,545 --> 00:28:53,905
Didn't I just mention him?

414
00:28:54,505 --> 00:28:55,905
Wu Shanlong.

415
00:29:08,065 --> 00:29:09,065
Hello?

416
00:29:09,145 --> 00:29:10,145
<i>Officer He,</i>

417
00:29:10,225 --> 00:29:11,945
<i>the video rental shop owner</i>
<i>you asked me to find</i>

418
00:29:12,025 --> 00:29:12,945
<i>has been arrested at the station.</i>

419
00:29:17,505 --> 00:29:20,785
PUBLIC SECURITY

420
00:29:27,745 --> 00:29:28,825
I'd like to ask,

421
00:29:28,905 --> 00:29:31,105
for producing obscene discs,

422
00:29:31,185 --> 00:29:32,625
how long would I be sentenced?

423
00:29:33,225 --> 00:29:35,745
If I provide clues
about the severed head case,

424
00:29:36,505 --> 00:29:38,225
would that count as meritorious service?

425
00:29:41,185 --> 00:29:42,545
Wu Zhengxiong.

426
00:29:42,625 --> 00:29:43,705
Whether it counts as meritorious service

427
00:29:43,785 --> 00:29:45,225
depends on whether
the information you provide

428
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:46,265
is actually useful.

429
00:29:46,345 --> 00:29:47,945
It'll definitely be useful.

430
00:29:48,585 --> 00:29:49,745
Back in '97,

431
00:29:49,825 --> 00:29:51,225
someone came to the video rental shop

432
00:29:51,305 --> 00:29:53,025
to hire Wolfie to kill someone.

433
00:29:53,105 --> 00:29:54,745
I took note of that person back then.

434
00:29:56,025 --> 00:29:56,985
Why didn't you report it at the time?

435
00:29:57,065 --> 00:29:58,105
Officer,

436
00:29:58,625 --> 00:30:00,105
I'm just an ordinary citizen.

437
00:30:00,825 --> 00:30:02,985
How would I dare
offend people from that world?

438
00:30:03,065 --> 00:30:05,705
Besides, I don't have nine lives.

439
00:30:05,785 --> 00:30:07,385
Cut the nonsense.

440
00:30:07,465 --> 00:30:08,745
Who was that person?

441
00:30:10,185 --> 00:30:12,505
Song Qingsong's brother-in-law,
Wu Shanlong.

442
00:30:12,585 --> 00:30:14,825
I saw him clearly back then.

443
00:30:14,905 --> 00:30:16,065
He was even driving that Mercedes

444
00:30:16,145 --> 00:30:18,145
with the license ending in 688.

445
00:30:19,105 --> 00:30:20,945
-Are you sure?
-I'm sure.

446
00:30:21,025 --> 00:30:23,305
Officer, I'm very good
at remembering faces.

447
00:30:23,385 --> 00:30:26,185
Back then, Jin Manshan
and his subordinate, Hu Anping,

448
00:30:26,265 --> 00:30:28,945
even took me to the entrance of Dahuihuang
to identify him in person.

449
00:30:32,185 --> 00:30:33,305
Officer,

450
00:30:33,825 --> 00:30:35,505
I've told you almost everything.

451
00:30:35,585 --> 00:30:37,105
About my case…

452
00:30:37,185 --> 00:30:39,145
-In this case…
-Han.

453
00:30:40,105 --> 00:30:42,105
-What is it, Officer He?
-Your turn.

454
00:30:42,185 --> 00:30:43,145
Alright.

455
00:30:43,225 --> 00:30:46,265
Officer, does this count
as meritorious service?

456
00:30:46,345 --> 00:30:48,105
-Officer.
-Sit down.

457
00:30:51,465 --> 00:30:53,145
He, let's go to Hongyun Huihuang Club.

458
00:30:53,225 --> 00:30:54,105
Let's go.

459
00:30:54,625 --> 00:30:55,585
Hold on.

460
00:30:58,745 --> 00:31:00,865
-What were those words?
-What does that mean?

461
00:31:01,905 --> 00:31:03,225
You take the lead, I'll back you up.

462
00:31:03,305 --> 00:31:05,585
You go upfront, I stay behind.
You play it clean, I handle the rough.

463
00:31:07,585 --> 00:31:09,105
What kind of coordination is that?

464
00:31:09,185 --> 00:31:10,345
Catching him is what matters.

465
00:31:10,425 --> 00:31:11,385
Let's go.

466
00:31:11,465 --> 00:31:13,425
I really can't believe this.

467
00:31:14,025 --> 00:31:15,505
In broad daylight,

468
00:31:15,585 --> 00:31:19,185
someone actually dares
to assault a law abiding citizen.

469
00:31:19,265 --> 00:31:20,665
And you're still sitting there?

470
00:31:20,745 --> 00:31:22,185
How are you enforcing the law?

471
00:31:22,265 --> 00:31:23,305
Why are you just sitting there?

472
00:31:23,385 --> 00:31:25,185
Go catch him.

473
00:31:25,705 --> 00:31:27,665
Do you have no sense of compassion at all?

474
00:31:27,745 --> 00:31:29,705
Look at this. You won't
even pour me a cup of tea.

475
00:31:29,785 --> 00:31:31,905
Is this how you treat an injured person?

476
00:31:34,425 --> 00:31:35,865
I came here to report a case,

477
00:31:36,625 --> 00:31:40,105
so why does it feel like
I'm the one being interrogated?

478
00:31:42,385 --> 00:31:44,945
You two officers,
aren't you criminal police?

479
00:31:45,025 --> 00:31:46,825
Why are you working at the station?

480
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:47,745
Wu Shanlong,

481
00:31:47,825 --> 00:31:49,585
you should know very well

482
00:31:49,665 --> 00:31:51,105
why we're here.

483
00:31:51,905 --> 00:31:53,305
I don't know. How would I know?

484
00:31:53,385 --> 00:31:54,665
You don't know?

485
00:31:54,745 --> 00:31:55,785
Fine.

486
00:31:55,865 --> 00:31:57,545
Start by explaining
what happened to your head.

487
00:31:58,825 --> 00:32:00,585
Someone tried to harm me.

488
00:32:00,665 --> 00:32:01,665
In broad daylight,

489
00:32:01,745 --> 00:32:03,985
he tried to smash my head open.

490
00:32:05,985 --> 00:32:08,145
Who tried to harm you? Tell it in detail.

491
00:32:08,225 --> 00:32:09,705
After we met yesterday,

492
00:32:09,785 --> 00:32:11,385
I was about to drive home.

493
00:32:11,465 --> 00:32:14,465
I don't know who put
a stone under my tire.

494
00:32:14,545 --> 00:32:16,025
So I got out, and when
I was moving that stone,

495
00:32:16,105 --> 00:32:18,265
suddenly, someone appeared behind me,

496
00:32:18,345 --> 00:32:19,545
and then bang,

497
00:32:21,465 --> 00:32:22,865
hit the back of my head.

498
00:32:22,945 --> 00:32:24,545
Luckily, I've trained
in martial arts before.

499
00:32:24,625 --> 00:32:25,465
My reflexes were fast.

500
00:32:25,545 --> 00:32:28,745
Otherwise, my head
would've been split in two.

501
00:32:28,825 --> 00:32:30,305
Was there anyone else at the scene?

502
00:32:32,065 --> 00:32:33,225
I left through the back door.

503
00:32:33,945 --> 00:32:35,225
No one saw anything.

504
00:32:38,545 --> 00:32:40,145
This is the weapon
the attacker left behind.

505
00:32:40,225 --> 00:32:41,465
Take it and run tests.

506
00:32:41,545 --> 00:32:43,705
The attacker's fingerprints must be on it.

507
00:32:44,305 --> 00:32:46,345
Right now, it's all
your fingerprints on it.

508
00:32:53,785 --> 00:32:55,705
Who do you think attacked you?

509
00:32:56,225 --> 00:32:57,465
I don't know who it was.

510
00:32:57,545 --> 00:32:58,825
Maybe someone saw
I was driving a Mercedes,

511
00:32:58,905 --> 00:33:01,545
thought I had money, and tried to rob me.

512
00:33:01,625 --> 00:33:04,545
After knocking me out,
they realized I was broke.

513
00:33:07,785 --> 00:33:09,145
Don't worry,

514
00:33:09,225 --> 00:33:10,945
we'll take this seriously.

515
00:33:11,025 --> 00:33:12,825
Do you have anything else to add?

516
00:33:16,105 --> 00:33:17,305
No.

517
00:33:24,065 --> 00:33:25,785
Then that's all.

518
00:33:25,865 --> 00:33:27,105
I can leave now, right?

519
00:33:27,185 --> 00:33:29,625
Who said you could leave?
We still have more questions.

520
00:33:29,705 --> 00:33:32,625
Repeat what you said yesterday
at Hongyun Huihuang Club.

521
00:33:32,705 --> 00:33:34,185
Didn't I already say it yesterday?

522
00:33:34,265 --> 00:33:35,865
-It's only been a day…
-Cut the nonsense.

523
00:33:35,945 --> 00:33:37,105
Say it.

524
00:33:40,545 --> 00:33:42,945
A few years ago,
Song Qingsong gave me 40,000

525
00:33:43,025 --> 00:33:44,745
to get rid of Xu Meng and her father.

526
00:33:44,825 --> 00:33:47,185
He may not know the law, but I do.
I couldn't possibly do what he asked…

527
00:33:47,265 --> 00:33:49,065
What you said doesn't match
your earlier statement.

528
00:33:53,385 --> 00:33:54,265
It's the same.

529
00:33:54,345 --> 00:33:55,665
There's no difference. It's the same.

530
00:33:56,545 --> 00:33:58,345
Song Qingsong, 40,000,

531
00:33:58,425 --> 00:34:00,065
Xu Meng and her father. I didn't do it.

532
00:34:00,145 --> 00:34:01,265
Then…

533
00:34:02,025 --> 00:34:03,345
Wu Shanlong,

534
00:34:03,865 --> 00:34:07,425
someone reported that you hired Wolfie
to kill Xu Meng and her father.

535
00:34:08,025 --> 00:34:09,545
Who said that? Who said it?

536
00:34:09,625 --> 00:34:10,665
That's slander.

537
00:34:10,744 --> 00:34:11,505
A false accusation.
This is clearly a frame up…

538
00:34:11,585 --> 00:34:12,905
Wu Shanlong.

539
00:34:13,585 --> 00:34:15,945
According to the Criminal Law
of the People's Republic of China,

540
00:34:16,025 --> 00:34:17,625
Articles 25 and 29,

541
00:34:17,705 --> 00:34:19,705
hiring someone to kill is punished

542
00:34:19,784 --> 00:34:21,505
as joint intentional homicide.

543
00:34:21,585 --> 00:34:23,784
The person who hires
is considered an instigator

544
00:34:23,865 --> 00:34:25,545
and bears primary criminal responsibility.

545
00:34:25,625 --> 00:34:27,824
That's impossible.
Someone must be framing me.

546
00:34:27,905 --> 00:34:29,385
-Impossible.
-Think carefully.

547
00:34:29,905 --> 00:34:32,505
Will you confess for leniency
or resist and face harsher punishment?

548
00:34:40,385 --> 00:34:41,264
Confess.

549
00:34:42,264 --> 00:34:43,425
I'll confess.

550
00:34:44,465 --> 00:34:46,185
I did hire Wolfie.

551
00:34:46,264 --> 00:34:47,985
Song Qingsong instructed

552
00:34:48,065 --> 00:34:50,385
that Xu Meng and her father
be driven out of Weiyang.

553
00:34:50,465 --> 00:34:52,304
I only meant to scare them away.

554
00:34:52,385 --> 00:34:54,065
I never intended to kill anyone.

555
00:34:54,145 --> 00:34:56,385
Besides, Wolfie never acted.

556
00:34:56,465 --> 00:34:57,985
-So…
-If Wolfie didn't act,

557
00:34:58,065 --> 00:34:59,625
then how did Xu Meng and her father die?

558
00:34:59,705 --> 00:35:01,705
-Did you hire someone else?
-No.

559
00:35:01,785 --> 00:35:03,745
-Or did you do it yourself?
-How could that be?

560
00:35:03,825 --> 00:35:05,705
It has nothing to do with me.
I didn't do anything.

561
00:35:06,705 --> 00:35:08,185
Stop playing tricks.

562
00:35:10,305 --> 00:35:11,745
I don't know anything anymore.

563
00:35:11,825 --> 00:35:13,905
I don't know anything now.
Go ask Song Qingsong.

564
00:35:13,985 --> 00:35:15,025
I don't know anything. Ask Song Qingsong.

565
00:35:15,105 --> 00:35:16,345
I want to go home now.

566
00:35:19,265 --> 00:35:21,025
Playing dumb,

567
00:35:21,105 --> 00:35:22,545
digging in his heels.

568
00:35:23,065 --> 00:35:25,705
He's definitely still hiding something.

569
00:35:25,785 --> 00:35:27,825
Since Wu Zhengxiong has pointed to him,

570
00:35:27,905 --> 00:35:30,465
then let's just detain him for 48 hours,

571
00:35:30,545 --> 00:35:32,505
wear him down, then press him again.

572
00:35:32,585 --> 00:35:33,865
He,

573
00:35:33,945 --> 00:35:36,505
Wu Shanlong came in as a reporting victim.

574
00:35:36,585 --> 00:35:38,345
We have no direct evidence

575
00:35:38,425 --> 00:35:39,585
and no detention warrant.

576
00:35:39,665 --> 00:35:41,825
If he keeps making a scene,

577
00:35:41,905 --> 00:35:43,305
we'll only end up more passive.

578
00:35:43,385 --> 00:35:45,265
Wait here. I'll go back
to the bureau and get one issued.

579
00:35:45,345 --> 00:35:46,505
Hold on.

580
00:35:47,345 --> 00:35:48,385
Let him go first.

581
00:35:48,465 --> 00:35:49,905
See what he does.

582
00:35:49,985 --> 00:35:52,465
If there really are accomplices
or anything hidden,

583
00:35:52,545 --> 00:35:54,585
once he's out, he'll make a move.

584
00:35:57,825 --> 00:35:59,025
I'm just angry.

585
00:35:59,545 --> 00:36:01,465
This guy has played us so many times,

586
00:36:01,545 --> 00:36:04,785
and now he's still out there living it up,

587
00:36:04,865 --> 00:36:06,585
free for five whole years.

588
00:36:08,065 --> 00:36:09,865
That's exactly why those
five years have cost us so much.

589
00:36:09,945 --> 00:36:11,425
Many clues and evidence

590
00:36:11,505 --> 00:36:12,945
are now hard to track down.

591
00:36:13,025 --> 00:36:15,305
We might as well let him show his hand,

592
00:36:15,385 --> 00:36:16,865
then use that chance to break through.

593
00:36:17,465 --> 00:36:19,505
Don't worry. I'll keep an eye on him.

594
00:36:20,705 --> 00:36:21,745
Then we cover both ends.

595
00:36:21,825 --> 00:36:23,185
I'll go find Jin Manshan

596
00:36:23,265 --> 00:36:25,145
and see if I can get anything out of him.

597
00:36:26,625 --> 00:36:28,825
Jin Manshan got involved
in organized crime three years ago

598
00:36:28,905 --> 00:36:29,945
and fled.

599
00:36:31,665 --> 00:36:33,185
The big one may run,

600
00:36:33,265 --> 00:36:34,225
but the small one won't.

601
00:36:39,945 --> 00:36:42,705
PUBLIC SECURITY

602
00:37:03,145 --> 00:37:04,385
Let's go to Yuanlongli.

603
00:37:26,625 --> 00:37:30,505
SWISH!

604
00:37:31,665 --> 00:37:33,145
BANG!

605
00:37:38,585 --> 00:37:39,745
Take a break.

606
00:37:40,265 --> 00:37:41,785
Eat while it's hot.

607
00:37:43,745 --> 00:37:44,705
I'll eat later.

608
00:37:44,785 --> 00:37:46,305
What do you mean later?

609
00:37:46,385 --> 00:37:48,785
By the time you remember,
I'll have cooked the next meal.

610
00:37:48,865 --> 00:37:49,865
I'm watching you.

611
00:37:49,945 --> 00:37:51,265
Eat it now.

612
00:38:01,145 --> 00:38:02,185
By the way,

613
00:38:02,705 --> 00:38:04,425
did that kid say anything today?

614
00:38:07,625 --> 00:38:08,865
He's developed acute stress.

615
00:38:08,945 --> 00:38:10,425
He hasn't said a word,

616
00:38:10,505 --> 00:38:11,825
completely shut himself off.

617
00:38:13,985 --> 00:38:14,905
Right now,

618
00:38:14,985 --> 00:38:17,465
I'm reading the comics he used to read,
trying to find a breakthrough.

619
00:38:18,345 --> 00:38:20,905
His mother said he usually just reads,

620
00:38:20,985 --> 00:38:22,185
doesn't play games or hang out online.

621
00:38:22,265 --> 00:38:24,025
I just can't figure out

622
00:38:24,105 --> 00:38:26,625
why he skipped school
and went to Yuanlongli.

623
00:38:26,705 --> 00:38:28,505
Times change.

624
00:38:28,585 --> 00:38:29,945
Energy is limited.

625
00:38:30,465 --> 00:38:32,145
Focus on the important.
Let go of the trivial.

626
00:38:32,225 --> 00:38:33,985
Food and clothing come first.

627
00:38:35,025 --> 00:38:36,025
What does that mean?

628
00:38:36,105 --> 00:38:38,785
It means when you investigate,

629
00:38:38,865 --> 00:38:40,505
you have to rely on common sense.

630
00:38:40,585 --> 00:38:42,745
What Han Zi'ang's mother said

631
00:38:42,825 --> 00:38:44,785
can't be taken at face value.

632
00:38:44,865 --> 00:38:47,105
That doesn't mean
she's lying to the police,

633
00:38:47,745 --> 00:38:50,265
but how many parents nowadays

634
00:38:50,345 --> 00:38:52,745
truly understand their children?

635
00:38:53,345 --> 00:38:55,745
Especially teenagers.

636
00:38:56,705 --> 00:38:57,945
Just like back then,

637
00:38:58,025 --> 00:38:59,145
you didn't understand me either.

638
00:39:00,585 --> 00:39:01,705
So,

639
00:39:01,785 --> 00:39:05,985
what Han Zi'ang's mother sees
may just be the side

640
00:39:06,065 --> 00:39:08,785
he wants her to see.

641
00:39:08,865 --> 00:39:10,985
Maybe Han Zi'ang

642
00:39:11,065 --> 00:39:13,385
does like gaming and hanging out online.

643
00:39:15,665 --> 00:39:16,505
That makes sense.

644
00:39:16,585 --> 00:39:18,625
At his age,

645
00:39:18,705 --> 00:39:20,265
legal internet cafes won't admit him.

646
00:39:20,345 --> 00:39:21,545
He can only go to unlicensed ones.

647
00:39:22,345 --> 00:39:25,345
But there aren't any in Yuanlongli.

648
00:39:25,425 --> 00:39:27,385
If you can find them,

649
00:39:28,385 --> 00:39:30,225
they wouldn't be unlicensed, would they?

650
00:39:33,745 --> 00:39:36,745
LASER ENGRAVING. CUSTOM GIFTS

651
00:39:46,425 --> 00:39:50,465
JUAN JUAN SHOE SHOP

652
00:39:50,545 --> 00:39:52,225
LIANG'S COMPUTER SUPPLIES

653
00:39:52,305 --> 00:39:53,145
Miss.

654
00:39:53,745 --> 00:39:54,825
Where's your boss?

655
00:39:55,745 --> 00:39:57,625
He stepped out.

656
00:39:57,705 --> 00:40:00,185
I've already asked this shop before.
No useful leads.

657
00:40:00,265 --> 00:40:01,345
Let's hurry and check the internet cafes.

658
00:40:07,065 --> 00:40:08,865
-Dad.
-Sir.

659
00:40:24,345 --> 00:40:25,745
Heal him.

660
00:40:27,585 --> 00:40:29,505
Druid, you can't heal?

661
00:40:31,545 --> 00:40:33,785
Uncle He, you scared me.

662
00:40:33,865 --> 00:40:35,745
At least say something first.

663
00:40:35,825 --> 00:40:36,905
You're the owner here, right?

664
00:40:38,745 --> 00:40:40,225
Why are you running
an illegal internet cafe

665
00:40:40,305 --> 00:40:41,705
and letting minors play games?

666
00:40:42,305 --> 00:40:43,625
Officer?

667
00:40:43,705 --> 00:40:44,745
Officer, you've misunderstood.

668
00:40:44,825 --> 00:40:45,945
I'm not running an illegal place.

669
00:40:46,025 --> 00:40:47,265
I have a license. A license?

670
00:40:47,345 --> 00:40:50,385
I just can't stand seeing kids
having nowhere to play.

671
00:40:50,465 --> 00:40:51,505
That's why I let them in.

672
00:40:51,585 --> 00:40:53,305
What I'm doing
is basically a public service.

673
00:40:53,385 --> 00:40:54,345
I don't charge anything.

674
00:40:54,425 --> 00:40:56,945
Really. I can swear on my game logs.

675
00:41:00,225 --> 00:41:02,545
Alright, don't make things hard for Du.

676
00:41:02,625 --> 00:41:05,705
He's an old acquaintance
of both me and your Uncle Ran.

677
00:41:05,785 --> 00:41:06,665
Really.

678
00:41:10,705 --> 00:41:11,625
Let me ask you again.

679
00:41:11,705 --> 00:41:13,105
Have you seen this kid?

680
00:41:15,505 --> 00:41:17,425
I already told you earlier,

681
00:41:17,505 --> 00:41:18,705
I haven't seen him.

682
00:41:20,185 --> 00:41:21,985
You can go ask outside.

683
00:41:26,745 --> 00:41:28,625
-Uncle He, your daughter
-Hey, boy.

684
00:41:28,705 --> 00:41:29,945
-is fierce.
-Excuse me.

685
00:41:30,025 --> 00:41:31,105
Have you seen this kid before?

686
00:41:31,185 --> 00:41:32,785
Takes after her dad.

687
00:41:32,865 --> 00:41:34,745
Born to be a criminal investigator.

688
00:41:35,345 --> 00:41:36,465
That's right.

689
00:41:36,545 --> 00:41:38,705
Hey, excuse me.

690
00:41:38,785 --> 00:41:39,905
Have you seen this kid?

691
00:41:39,985 --> 00:41:41,185
No.

692
00:41:42,465 --> 00:41:44,425
Hi. Have you seen this kid?

693
00:41:45,025 --> 00:41:46,065
No.

694
00:41:47,985 --> 00:41:49,105
Wait.

695
00:41:51,305 --> 00:41:52,785
I've seen him.

696
00:41:52,865 --> 00:41:56,065
Last week, he was at that computer
watching role playing stuff,

697
00:41:56,145 --> 00:41:57,265
laughing while watching,

698
00:41:57,345 --> 00:41:59,145
even speaking some Japanese.

699
00:41:59,225 --> 00:42:01,305
Definitely a hardcore anime fan.

700
00:42:01,945 --> 00:42:03,545
Pull up photos of those four kids.

701
00:42:04,425 --> 00:42:06,025
Excuse me. Can I use your computer?

702
00:42:13,585 --> 00:42:15,625
These four, have you seen them?

703
00:42:16,905 --> 00:42:17,745
Haven't seen them.

704
00:42:17,825 --> 00:42:19,185
What about you? Have you seen them?

705
00:42:23,505 --> 00:42:24,425
This one, I've seen.

706
00:42:24,505 --> 00:42:25,665
SPREAD THE NEWS: THESE KIDS ARE MISSING

707
00:42:25,745 --> 00:42:27,225
This one, I've seen too.

